WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.914
Welcome to Module 6 of the
Non-Person Identity learning path:

2
00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:06.850
Conditional Access for
workload identities.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.199
This module is the Conditional
Access half of Gate 4,

4
00:00:10.199 --> 00:00:13.938
Least privilege, with Chapter
8 of the developer workbook.

5
00:00:13.938 --> 00:00:18.469
You'll hold the program's two
workload policies as reviewed files,

6
00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:20.651
scoped by object I D, ring by ring.

7
00:00:20.651 --> 00:00:22.708
You'll check them before they merge,

8
00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:26.825
plan them against a fictional tenant,
and create every one report-only.

9
00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:29.512
Then you'll read the
service principal sign-ins,

10
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:32.889
and see a ring enforced only
when a person has reviewed them,

11
00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:37.575
the security chief has recorded the decision,
and the change explicitly allows it.

12
00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:40.812
The code runs on your laptop
against a fictional tenant.

13
00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:45.890
It's illustrative: tested against
fixtures, not run against a live tenant.
